  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14274266/assets/1083b3341f9ee7105c3df7dbcf896ab89e6afcfbe3bc9a4ec837d24df8b4dd8f.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,7].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $6,$ $9,$ and $4,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,7]$ given that $f(-2)=1.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
